I left out the enrichment fetch. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/state-rw`, so it has no `http-client` import, and the fetch would send digest contents to an external host. The body below records each considered id under the `seen` store, with the run date as the value.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{published-digest, run-report};
    import aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0;
    export run: func(published: published-digest) -> run-report;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(published: PublishedDigest) -> RunReport {
        let mut recorded: u32 = 0;
        for id in &published.considered {
            crate::aap::caps::state_rw::put(id, &published.date);
            recorded = recorded.saturating_add(1);
        }
        RunReport {
            date: published.date,
            recorded,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

